course: dictionary
lesson: 5360
title: Kingdom: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives three meanings for kingdom, and the words around it show you which one is being used. «London, on the River Thames, is the capital of the United Kingdom.» Here kingdom is part of a country's name, so it means a country ruled by a king or queen.
explain: In «the animal kingdom», kingdom means a big group that living things are sorted into in science. Animals are one group, and plants are another group, called «the plant kingdom». Try the first meaning in this phrase and it does not fit: animals are not ruled by a king.
explain: The third meaning is a playful one. «The kitchen is Dad's kingdom» means the kitchen is an area that belongs to Dad. Try swapping in your meaning: "the kitchen is Dad's country" makes no sense, so this meaning must be the right one.
fact: Kingdom means a country ruled by a king or queen.
fact: In science, a kingdom is one of the big groups that living things are sorted into, like the animal kingdom and the plant kingdom.
fact: «The United Kingdom» is the name of a country, and London is its capital.
fact: «In 221 BC the king of Qin conquered all the warring kingdoms and called himself the First Emperor.» Here the kingdoms were separate countries that fought each other.
fact: Kingdoms often appear in fairy tales, with castles, kings and queens.
exercise: «In 1337, England and Scotland were separate rival kingdoms.» What does kingdom mean in this sentence? | A group of living things | A castle wall | *A country ruled by a king or queen | A kitchen or a room that belongs to someone
exercise: In science, what is «the animal kingdom»? | *A big group that animals are sorted into | A castle with a moat | A country on a map | A king's bedroom
exercise: «The kitchen is Dad's kingdom.» What does kingdom mean here? | A country ruled by a king | A tiny mustard seed | A group of plants | *An area that belongs to someone
test: In «the plant kingdom», what does kingdom mean? | A rule of kings and queens | *A big group of living things | A small garden | A king's palace
test: Which of these was a kingdom in the given sentences? | A mustard seed | Dad's kitchen | *Castile | A village on a river
exam: Why does kingdom mean something different in «the animal kingdom» than in «the United Kingdom»? | Because kingdom always means a country | *Because the words around it change the meaning: one is a science group, and the other is a country | Because the spelling changes between sentences | Because animals have kings
